      "message": "When testing 6.12 patches, I ran into issue guest was receiving EFAULT when guest touches the mapped page.\n\n   Step 2: EL2 Hypervisor Page State Check (mem_protect.c)\n\n  The hypercall enters EL2:\n\n    __pkvm_host_donate_guest() (mem_protect.c)\n       │\n       ├──\u003e ___host_check_page_state_range(phys, size, PKVM_PAGE_OWNED, ...)\n       │       └──\u003e Returns -EPERM because page is marked PKVM_MODULE_OWNED_PAGE (4), not PKVM_PAGE_OWNED (0)\n       │\n       └──\u003e [Handles -EPERM]: Calls ___pkvm_module_share_guest()\n               │\n               └──\u003e ___pkvm_check_module_share_guest() (mem_protect.c:2424)\n                       │\n                       ├──\u003e Check 1: ___host_check_page_state_range(phys, size, state, ...)\n                       │       └──\u003e Lines 1120-1122:\n                       │            p \u003d hyp_phys_to_page(addr);\n                       │            if (p-\u003ehost_state !\u003d state)\n                       │                return -EPERM;\n                       │\n                       │            • Actual p-\u003ehost_state in memory \u003d 4 (PKVM_MODULE_OWNED_PAGE)\n                       │            • Old code passed: state \u003d 8 | 4 \u003d 12 (PKVM_NOPAGE | PKVM_MODULE_OWNED_PAGE)\n                       │            • 4 !\u003d 12 EVALUATED TO TRUE -\u003e Returned -EPERM -\u003e Returned -EFAULT (14)!\n                       │\n                       │            [CHANGE 2]: Passing PKVM_MODULE_OWNED_PAGE (4).\n                       │                        4 !\u003d 4 is FALSE -\u003e Check 1 PASSES!\n                       │\n                       ├──\u003e Check 2: __guest_check_page_state_range(..., PKVM_NOPAGE | PKVM_ACCEPT_MODULE_OWNED)\n                       │       └──\u003e Matches annotation from SMC 0x123 -\u003e Check 2 PASSES!\n                       │\n                       └──\u003e Check 3: module_guest_accept_module_owned_share()\n                               └──\u003e Calls example_heap module callback (returns 0) -\u003e Check 3",
